- op: discuss  # 5dc7
  at: '2026-10-18T10:59:49Z'  # 5dc7
  by: agent  # 5dc7
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5dc7
  clock: 3  # 5dc7
  nonce: 5dc7  # 5dc7
  message: "Fixed in PR #1716 (dev d2f7d0bba0). websocket.py: sites take their event from the shared _name_args resolver (name_arg_from_match; same-file module-scope string constant -> 'constant', else 'unresolved'); pair_by_name replaces the raw-string grouping; edge meta event = joined value or None, event_type = join kind, event_identifier = identifier of an identifier join; channel = join.channel. http.py: _extract_url_from_match resolves bare identifiers through the same resolver at every scanner (python, js/ts, go, java; ruby has no resolver rules so stays unresolved); a constant is route-matched and scored as a literal (0.9 / 0.8 cross-language); an unresolved identifier gets url_path None on its client symbol and is never route-matched. DECISION requested by the item: http's JS-only _extract_module_constants (template-literal folding) was NOT replaced -- fold_string_interpolation takes a name->value map for all slots, its rule is the one WI-sijoh measured, and the resolver's stricter rebinding checks would change template matching unmeasured; recorded in its docstring. LIVE REPRO on dev d2f7d0bba0 (link_websocket / link_http on a 3-file fixture): sender.js 'const EVENT = \"chat\"; socket.emit(EVENT)' + 'function relay(note, p) { socket.emit(note, p) }', receiver.js 'socket.on(\"chat\")' + 'socket.on(\"note\")' -> exactly one event_publishes edge, sender->receiver, event='chat', event_type='constant', 0.85 (before: EVENT never joined 'chat', and the parameter note DID join 'note'). client.js 'const API_URL = \"/api/users\"; fetch(API_URL); fetch(OTHER_URL)' with routes '/api/users' and 'OTHER_URL' -> client API_URL: url '/api/users', url_type 'constant', edge to the /api/users route at 0.9; client OTHER_URL: url_type 'unresolved', url_path None, no edge (before: API_URL matched nothing; OTHER_URL text matched the route named OTHER_URL). Production-path tests: test_websocket.py TestVariableEventPatterns (test_a_constant_joins_the_literal_it_names, test_an_identifier_never_matches_a_string_of_the_same_text, test_unresolved_identifiers_join_on_the_identifier, test_constant_events_join_on_their_value) and test_http_linker.py (test_a_constant_url_resolves_and_matches_its_route, test_an_unresolved_identifier_is_not_route_matched, test_go_const_url_resolves, test_java_static_final_url_resolves). NOT measured: corpus frequency of either shape (the item also left it unmeasured)."  # 5dc7
